Colo. Rev. Stat. § 12-245-603
Practice of licensed professional counseling defined
(1) For purposes of this part 6, “practice of licensed
professional counseling” means the application of
mental health, psychological, or human development
principles through cognitive, affective, behavioral, or
systematic intervention strategies that address
wellness, personal growth, or career development, as
well as pathology. A licensed professional counselor
may render the application of these principles to
individuals, couples, families, or groups.
(2) The practice of professional counseling may
include:
(a) Evaluation;
(b) Assessment;
(c) Testing;
(d) Diagnosis;
(e) Treatment or intervention;
(f) Planning;
(g) Consultation;
(h) Case management;
(i) Education;
(j) Supervision;
(k) Psychotherapy;
(l) Research;
(m) Referral; and
(n) Crisis intervention.

